<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Catalaunian Plains</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">451</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Châlons</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Catalaunian Plains was fought in 451 in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> between the Hunnic army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> and a coalition led by the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> and the Visigothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-i">Theodoric I</a>. Theodoric was killed, but Attila withdrew from Gaul. It was one of the last great campaigns of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains.jpg" alt="Battle of the Catalaunian Plains" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes de Thurocz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thur%C3%B3czy_kr%C3%B3nika_-_Attila_kir%C3%A1ly_csat%C3%A1ja_a_catalaunumi_s%C3%ADkon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
